 # Implemented method and limits
 
-The native method is a supplied-input corporate surveillance assembly. It recomputes gross/net leverage, interest coverage and an EBITDA-minus-capex over interest proxy; compares comparable prior metrics; reports an instrument spread delta and agency rating/outlook changes; and flags supplied covenant changes. It does not establish a complete issuer view, internal rating, investment thesis, funding access, security value, covenant headroom, DSCR, recovery, market-implied credit view, portfolio decision or legal conclusion. Sovereign, public-finance, structured-credit, bank and insurance specialist engines are not supplied by these formulas.
+The only live implementation is the supplied-evidence method described in [analytical rules](phase2-rules.md) and [schema](phase2-schema.md). It compares source-bound corporate reported leverage, interest coverage, a fixed-charge proxy, supplied available liquidity to known maturities, eligible spread observations and reported events.
 
-Gross/net debt-to-EBITDA is withheld for nonpositive EBITDA. Coverage divides by positive interest expense only. `fccr_x` is explicitly the (EBITDA − capex) / interest proxy, not contractual FCCR or DSCR. Cash is available only with confirmed supplied accessibility; revolver only with confirmed supplied availability. Restricted or conditional funding stays nominal, with available total null. A complete dated maturity inventory is required for full scheduled near-term total. `known_near_term_maturities` is a labeled subtotal. `maturity_funding_comparison` covers scheduled maturities only; past-due amounts or incomplete coverage withhold it. `liquidity_covers_near_term` stays null because operating uses, contingent needs and refinancing feasibility are absent.
+Gross/net debt-to-EBITDA requires positive EBITDA; coverage requires positive interest. The fixed-charge measure is `(EBITDA - mandatory_capex) / interest_expense`, not contractual FCCR or DSCR. The liquidity measure is `(unrestricted_cash + available_committed_facilities) / near_term_maturities`, requiring positive maturities and a supplied complete inventory. It does not assess all operating/contingent uses, restricted cash, refinancing feasibility or funding access. Obtain a separately validated capital-structure/maturity method when instrument-level maturity detail is required.
 
-Maturities require instrument ID, legal issuer ID, matching currency, amount, source and exact-date/year consistency. Repeated instrument rows require consolidation in a reviewed adapter. Spreads must reference a market source and identified instrument/issuer, spread type and currency. Agency opinions must reference a rating-agency source and identify issuer vs instrument object; the packet assigns no rating. Covenant flags require instrument/document/version. Source-type mismatches fail before computation. Approval person/role strings are assertions; distinct preparer/reviewer labels do not authenticate people.
+Financial observations must use comparable duration, fiscal calendar, currency, units, accounting basis and consolidation scope and end no later than economic as-of and the cutoff date. Source knowledge is separate from economic period. No forecast/scenario or specialist bank/insurer conversion is inferred.
 
-Economic dates/forecast periods do not establish when information was known. Where this native contract uses an intraday cutoff, source knowledge timestamps require timezones. A source reference and a reproducible hash do not prove content authenticity or licensed use.
+Source-bound quotes require the observation, mapping and freshness controls in the analytical schema; a current source timestamp cannot date an unknown quote. Missing/inconsistent evidence withholds dependent measures. Full reconstruction detects changed/extra/removed output or a substituted original. Source assertions and hashes do not authenticate facts, licensed use or professional approval.
+
+The legacy packet assembly is retired. Use [reviewed migration](schema.md); do not execute historical source as a production fallback or reinterpret old success fixtures as current eligibility evidence.
